Fix build with GCC 15 (default -std=gnu23), where glibc's strchr() is
const-preserving: calling it on `const char *tapeprefix` returns
`const char *`, which this code assigned to plain `char *`, failing
under -Werror=discarded-qualifiers. In tape.c the code also wrote a
'\0' through that pointer, so the volume-list splitting is rewritten
to split without modifying the const string.

--- a/dump/main.c
+++ b/dump/main.c
@@ -498,7 +498,7 @@
 
 	{
 		int i;
-		char *n;
+		const char *n;
 
 		if ((n = strchr(tapeprefix, ':'))) {
 			for (i = 0; i < (n - tapeprefix); i++) {
